  An amulet of life saving can only save your life once, and whatever killed
your character the first time will generally still be around to kill your
character again.  (Character death due to a typo may alert the player to be more
careful.  Then again, it may not.)

  The "random" lightning you encounter on the Plane of Air only occurs in the
clouds.  It's not an electric attack.  Instead it paralyzes you for some number
of turns.  Ring of free action doesn't protect against the paralysis.  Neither
does shock resistance.

  The extra AC of the shield of reflection will help against almost every attack
you meet in the Endgame.   Lower AC can help save your life again and again.
That it gives reflection so you can wear an amulet of life saving is a bonus,
but not the main point.


  Wands of polymorph are one solution to the problem of air elementals, e.g.:

<http://www.melankolia.net/nethack/nethack.fun.html#12>

  (It's funny.  It's also true.)


Here's another method of dealing with air elementals, from
<http://www.spod-central.org/~psmith/nh/wan1-343.txt>:

slow monster (BEAM)
  zap monster
    The monster becomes slow, or normal speed if fast.  If you are engulfed
    by a vortex or air elemental, you are expelled.  Some monsters may
    resist.
      "You disrupt <monster>! A huge hole opens up..." (expelled)
      "<Monster> seems to be moving slower." (slowed, not swallowed)



  (Bet you didn't think wands of polymorph and slow monster could be critical
Endgame items.)


  Players on the Ascension Run with amulet(s) of life saving tend to either use
all of them, and die anyway, or they don't use any of them, and Ascend.  Perhaps
not always true, but close.


  There's no one solution to the Endgame.  That's why it's so tough.  A number
of non-obvious items can be critical to your survival.  And once you exit the
dungeon, you can't go back to your stash.  You're fleeing forward in Alpine
mode.  All you've got is what you're carrying with you.  Neglect one critical
item and it's all over.

  Even lower AC isn't "the" solution.  Lower AC combined with ring of free
action, ring of conflict, and invisibility + displacement minimizes the number
of hits you take, as well as the damage from each hit.

  Wands of polymorph and/or slow monster further reduce the hits you take from
the hardest hitters in the Endgame: air elementals.

