  And most of the escape methods used in the Dungeon no longer work:

     - wand/spell of digging zapped downward won't drop you through a hole.
     - c!oGL won't take you up a level
     - #invoking Orb of Fate or the Eye of Aethiopica won't level teleport.
     - Can't engrave Elbereth on the Air/Water Planes.  The Riders and the As
       on the Astral Plane don't respect Elbereth.
     - Cursed/confused scroll of teleport won't take you to another level.
     - Can't self-teleport on the level.
     - Can't immediately go back up/down the stairs
     - Scrolls of earth no longer work: no instant fort.
     - b?oGeno won't work on the most dangerous monsters: E, @, A, &, etc.


  It's like starting up a new game in that, just like for a starting character,
there's no one technique/item you can absolutely rely on to keep you alive.
You can't deal out damage fast enough.  You don't have the hit points necessary
to survive a lot of melee combat, and your AC doesn't protect you enough.
You're back to avoiding melee combat as much as possible and killing things from
a distance when you have to kill. 

  You've got to rely on defense in depth and still use every trick in the book.
And, just like starting a new character, there's no stash of goodies you can go
visit to get something you need.

  The constantly resurrecting Riders of the Apocalypse are like when you
encounter trolls for the first time in the dungeon, except it's very difficult
to get rid of the Riders permanently.

  The good news is that there's sanctuary out there: A co-aligned high altar you
can sacrifice the AoY at.  And there's a way to make more than one of the high
altars on Astral usable for that purpose.



  The best AC you can get probably won't be enough, by itself, to get yo
through.  But AC is still your first line of defense.  Free action keeps you
from being paralyzed.  Conflict distracts monsters from focusing on you.
Invisibility/displacement makes it easier to slip past monsters who are trying
to hit you.  Wands of teleport for when the way is completely blocked.
Levitation to control your movements on the Plane of Air.  Jumping for ultra
fast travel on the Plane of Fire and the Astral Plane.  Levitation to make
travel on the Plane of Water safer and easier.

  And you still want to use every possible trick available to you.  Down to
wishing for a blessed cockatrice corpse.


  You may well want to try the Endgame in wizard mode, just for practice.




